            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "With this setup `autowrite` is most certainly works as expected and respects `directory`.\r\n\r\nWhat `autowrite = true` does is that it [saves **current** (a.k.a. loaded/read) session](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f54410c7f866f51711118fd82274043cf731b63d/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L80) before quitting Neovim. That is, it uses `MiniSessions.write(nil, { force = true })` which [writes to the `v:this_session` path](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f54410c7f866f51711118fd82274043cf731b63d/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L162-L163).\r\n\r\nSo if the observed behavior is that it is written session at '/home/USER/.local/state/nvim/sessions/autosession.vim', then that session was current just before quitting Neovim.\r\n\r\nGenerally, for `autowrite = true` to be useful there should be session either `read()` first or created/initiated with a call to `write()`. It is designed this way to not spam session files when Neovim is opened for quick editing.\r\n\r\nClosing as (most certainly) not an issue with 'mini.sessions'.\r\n______\r\n\r\nI would also suggest using `vim.fn.stdpath('state')` instead of `vim.fn.expand('$XDG_STATE_HOME') .. '/nvim'` as it is more portable (doesn't require `XDG_STATE_HOME` to actually be defined) and concise.",
