        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Perhaps documentation could be changed to clarify this behaviour?\r\n\r\nPrior to `mini.sessions`, I have used the following routine:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nsession_file_path = vim.fn.expand(\"$XDG_STATE_HOME\")\r\n                    .. \"/nvim/sessions/\" .. \"autosession.vim\"\r\n \r\nMakeSession = function()\r\n  vim.api.nvim_command(\"mksession! \" .. session_file_path)\r\nend\r\n \r\nLoadSession = function()\r\n  if io.open(session_file_path, \"r\") then\r\n    vim.api.nvim_command(\"source \" .. session_file_path)\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"VimLeave\", {\r\n    desc = \"Create autosession on exit\",\r\n    callback = function()\r\n        MakeSession()\r\n    end\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n...and it worked just fine, especially in conjunction with:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nalias rv=\"nvim -S $XDG_STATE_HOME/nvim/sessions/autosession.vim\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow, trying to replicate the same via `mini.sessions` is less straightforward than expected.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n**P.S.** Appreciate the tip re. `vim.fn.stdpath('state')`!",
