        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "After some further reading of the documentation, I have ended-up with this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal sessions = require('mini.sessions')\r\n\r\nsessions.setup({\r\n\r\n    autoread = false,\r\n    autowrite = true,\r\n    directory = vim.fn.stdpath('state') .. \"/sessions/\",\r\n    file = 'autosession',\r\n\r\n    force = {\r\n        delete = false,\r\n        read = false,\r\n        write = true,\r\n    },\r\n    verbose = {\r\n        delete = true,\r\n        read = false,\r\n        write = false,\r\n    },\r\n\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.keymap.set(\r\n    'n',\r\n    '<leader>sw',\r\n    function()\r\n        vim.ui.input({ prompt = 'Write session:' }, function(response)\r\n            if string.len(response) > 0 then\r\n                sessions.write(response)\r\n            else\r\n                sessions.write('autosession')\r\n            end\r\n        end)\r\n    end,\r\n    { desc = 'Write session' }\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nDoes the job, might help someone else who finds this issue.",
