            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> If I understand correctly, the behavior that worked just fine is a \"have single session be read during startup and written before closing Neovim\".\r\n\r\nNot quite. The desired behaviour is to _\"save session on each exit and allow user to load it afterwards\"_.\r\n\r\nFor reasons unknown, even with `autowrite = true` I wasn't able to reliably reproduce this simple routine.\r\n\r\n",
