        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> For reasons unknown, even with `autowrite = true` I wasn't able to reliably reproduce this simple routine.\r\n\r\nReasons were already given: `autowrite = true` saves only if session (as in Neovim's/Vim's session) is in use at the moment of closing. This is determined by `vim.g.this_session` global variable.\r\n\r\nTo *always* save to same session before closing Neovim, make own autocommand. With something like this:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.sessions').setup({ autowrite = false })\r\nlocal make_omnisession = function() MiniSessions.write('omnisession', { force = true }) end\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('VimLeavePre', { callback = make_omnisession, desc = 'Make omnisession' })\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2024-01-25T09:48:39Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/655#issuecomment-1909775813",
            "id": 1909775813,
