        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I've been reading a couple of this issues and I believe there's a fundamental misunderstanding on this.\r\n\r\nI find myself in a similar situation, whereas mini.sessions work, but not as I would expect. That's the workflow of the issue:\r\n\r\n- Open some buffers in Neovim\r\n- Save a new session with mini.sessions\r\n- Close Neovim\r\n\r\n- Reopen Neovim\r\n- Load the saved session (it woks fine)\r\n- While working it the \"session\" close some buffers, open some other\r\n- Close Neovim\r\n\r\n- Reopen and load the same session\r\n\r\nAt this point I can only restore the very first created version of said session, as in, when I closed and opened some buffers and then closed neovim, mini.sessions didn't overwrite the session's file with the new state.\r\n\r\nI thought this plugin would keep track on the buffers I open and close on a certain \"session\" of work.\r\n\r\nAt least this is what I would expect. ",
