        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> * Load the saved session (it woks fine)\r\n> \r\n> * While working it the \"session\" close some buffers, open some other\r\n> \r\n> * Close Neovim\r\n> \r\n> * Reopen and load the same session\r\n>\r\n> At this point I can only restore the very first created version of said session, as in, when I closed and opened some buffers and then closed neovim, mini.sessions didn't overwrite the session's file with the new state.\r\n\r\nYes, it does restore the state of session as it was prior to the last closing Neovim (i.e. after \"close some buffers, open some other\"). I've just double checked.\r\n\r\nThe option that controls if 'mini.sessions' automatically overrides current session file (that is, loaded with `MiniSessions.read()` or in other way that sets `vim.v.this_session`) is [`config.autowrite`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/70d8a16399ca6df759d20bea302d6dfd710a1df8/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L80-L81). It is `true` by default so should work with default config. What config do you use?",
