        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) is there a way to store the session file using an absolute path?\n> \n> local file = vim.fn.stdpath(\"state\")\n> \t.. vim.fn.fnamemodify(vim.fn.getcwd(), \":t\")\n> \t.. \".vim\"\n> \n> as the path doesn't work for example. It gets annoying having to ignore the file each time i create the session with gitignore\n\nYes. By storing global session named `vim.fn.fnamemodify(vim.fn.getcwd(), \":t\") .. '.vim'`. So something like this:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.sessions').setup({\n  directory = vim.fn.stdpath('state'),\n  file = '',\n})\n```\n\nAnd later execute `:lua MiniSessions.write(vim.fn.fnamemodify(vim.fn.getcwd(), \":t\") .. '.vim')`.\n\nThe `config.file` is specifically for [local sessions](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4dd209e4f03bacd46d6d87408b2529a8823112fb/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L18), i.e. for files inside current working directory.",
